 **one declared exception** to the stdlib-only rule (optional `pywinpty`, lazily imported, degrades gracefully if absent).\n\n- **It is self-verifying** â€” `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file, exercising every API endpoint, and walking the fully-stubbed v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (never touching the live `:8777` service or real data), writing dated reports and surfacing failures as a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **Branding/positioning:** presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" with a vendored brand mark used as favicon and masthead.\n\n**In one line:** Anchor is a markdown-backed personal task/project dashboard that has evolved into a local mission-control for driving and remembering AI agent-trio R&D work â€” shipped as a persistently-running, self-healthchecking, stdlib-only Python web app on `localhost:8777`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e23e3ed5-d33d-4b48-908c-2769a502d362","uuid":"e7cb4fe8-9f18-4f4a-83ff-ff3e98049432","request_id":"req_011Cc1iCHUjkAbnBDsq5KTuL"}
